<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>hr.hrg.jcodebuddy</groupId>
        <artifactId>jcodebuddy-parent</artifactId>
        <version>1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
        <relativePath>../../pom.xml</relativePath>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>jcodebuddy-watch-tools</artifactId>
    <name>JCodeBuddy Watch Tools</name>
    <description>
        JCodeBuddy's code actions for the watcher: tools a launcher registers into java-watch-agent's
        ToolRegistry. It exists because the watcher must not know about JCodeBuddy — `java-watch*` depends on
        no Jackson, no OpenRewrite and nothing else from this workspace (DEC-038's amendment, plan step 3.0s)
        — while these tools are JCodeBuddy work: they drive `jwa-builder` to read a Java type out of source
        and complete it.
    </description>

    <!--
        WHY THIS MODULE EXISTS, AND WHY IT IS NOT `project-automation`.

        The obvious home for a bridge between the watcher's ActionTool port and jwa-builder is
        `project-automation`, which already depends on both — and it is **forbidden**: no other module may
        depend on a `project-automation` (AGENTS.md § 1.1), and a launcher would have to, in order to register
        a tool. So the bridge is a small library instead, which the app may depend on.

        The direction is the honest one: this module depends on `java-watch-agent` (for the ActionTool port),
        never the other way round. The watcher knows a directory changed; this module knows what to do about a
        Java file.
    -->

    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>hr.hrg.jcodebuddy</groupId>
            <artifactId>java-watch-agent</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>hr.hrg.jcodebuddy</groupId>
            <artifactId>java-watch-core</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>hr.hrg.jcodebuddy</groupId>
            <artifactId>jwa-builder</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>hr.hrg.jcodebuddy</groupId>
            <artifactId>jwa-builder-api</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.slf4j</groupId>
            <artifactId>slf4j-api</artifactId>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>
</project>
